[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### One divergence found and fixed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows 15–17 (null `struct ConfigFlags*`) diverged in the **debug** build profile:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m DIVERGENCE [err15]: C died as Signaled(11), Rust died as Signaled(6)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C dereferences the caller's pointer with no null check, so a null argument
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is a hardware fault — SIGSEGV. The Rust used a plain `*(flags as *const u8)`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m raw-pointer dereference, which rustc instruments under `debug_assertions` with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m a null-pointer check that panics (`null pointer dereference occurred`) and, in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m a `cdylib`, aborts — SIGABRT. The release `.so` matched, so this was invisible
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m until the suite was run against the debug-profile artifact.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Fix (`src/lib.rs`, `read_flags` / `write_flags`): use `core::ptr::read` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `core::ptr::write` instead of `*ptr` / `*ptr = …`. Those carry no null check in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m any profile and fault exactly like the C. Verified empirically that `*p`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m aborts under `debug_assertions` while `ptr::read(p)` segfaults, in both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m profiles. Reverting the fix reproduces the failure, so the guard is genuinely
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m tested rather than vacuous.
